# Query Optimization

Reference: `.cursor/architecture/indexing-matrix.md`

## Forbidden in Production
```php
// ❌ SELECT *
Student::all();

// ❌ N+1
$enrollments = Enrollment::all();
foreach ($enrollments as $e) { $e->student; }

// ❌ Unbounded queries
Attendance::where('school_id', $id)->get(); // no date limit
```

## Required Patterns
```php
// ✅ Select only needed columns
Student::select(['id', 'student_code', 'full_name'])->...

// ✅ Eager load
Enrollment::with(['student:id,full_name', 'section'])->...

// ✅ Paginate or cursor
Enrollment::where('academic_year_id', $yearId)->cursorPaginate(50);

// ✅ Scope by academic year always
Attendance::forAcademicYear($yearId)->where('student_id', $id)->...
```

## Cache Reference Data
```php
Cache::remember("schools.{$directorateId}", 3600, fn () =>
    School::where('directorate_id', $directorateId)->where('status', 1)->get()
);
```

## Before Adding an Index
1. Identify slow query via logs/monitoring
2. Run EXPLAIN ANALYZE
3. Check if existing index covers it
4. Add index via migration
5. Re-measure

## Bulk Operations
```php
// ✅ Batch insert
Student::insert($rows); // chunks of 500

// ✅ Queue for 1000+ records
ImportStudentsJob::dispatch($filePath, $idempotencyKey);
```

## Reports
Dashboard reads from materialized views or cached aggregates — not live JOINs across 10+ OLTP tables.
